# What must never enter the image.
#
# The one ignore file for both tools. Docker reads only `.dockerignore`;
# podman reads `.containerignore` first and falls back to this file when it is
# absent (verified with podman 5.8.9, 2026-10-22). So there must be no
# `.containerignore`: podman would prefer it, and a copy missing a line below
# would `COPY . .` the `.env` — the bot token, the Discord client secret and
# the Twitch credentials — into an image layer a later `RUN rm` cannot reach.
# That is the failure that succeeds rather than erroring, so
# `tests/test_configuration_security.py` asserts this file exists and the other
# does not.
#
# The build does `COPY . .`, so anything left lying in a working tree would
# otherwise be baked in — the same reason the publisher derives its snapshot
# from `git ls-files` rather than from disk.
.git
.env
# The database container's superuser password (compose's `db` service).
.env.postgres
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db.backup*
# A pg_dump is every member's data, wherever it was left.
*.dump
backups/
logs/
venv/
.venv/
.claude/
dashboard-reference/
.local-dev/
# The generated session-signing secret. Baking it in would ship one
# installation's key to every image built from this tree.
.dashboard_session_secret
# Game icons: uploaded to Discord by hand, read by no code, other people's
# artwork. The bot's own avatar lives at the repository root and does ship.
botdata/
# Compiled bytecode is rebuilt in the image and only bloats the layer.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Local working files that `.gitignore` already keeps out of the repository
# and that a `COPY . .` from a working tree would otherwise bake in: session
# notes, the knowledge graph, screenshots of the live dashboard, rehearsal
# copies of a database, the Everydle deck and the drafted guild message.
handoff/
graphify-out/
Screenshot*.png
migration-rehearsal-*/
data/everydle_state.json
docs/guild_message.md
node_modules/
*.log
.aider*
